== Trivia ==
*Not long before the leak of the information of new collections of Crimson Isle update about Mycelium and Red Sand collections, the ability of obtaining Mycelium, including spreading onto dirt and buying from trades menu, were removed. This was likely for preventing stockpiling by alpha testers.
**As {{zone|Crimson Isle}} released on [[Changelog/2022/April 20|April 20, 2022]], mycelium spreading onto dirt has been re-enabled.
*Using a {{Item|Builder's Ruler}} or {{Item|Block Zapper}} to remove mycelium will turn it into dirt, with the following message: {{Dialogue|&eYour &a# &fMycelium &ehas turned into &fDirt&e!}}
**This happens even on {{zone|The Garden}}, where mycelium spread is disabled.
*Collecting Mycelium turned from {{Item|Dirt}} on Private Islands '''does''' increase collection, that is unless the dirt block was placed by a player.
** However, there are only limited ways to have Mycelium giving collection on the island: the initial island (turn {{Item|Grass}} blocks to dirt by placing blocks right onto them), some type of placeable islands, and {{Item|Mycelium Minion}}s.
* Contrary to the low light level requirement of {{Item|Mushroom}} spreading, Mycelium requires high light level to spread onto dirt.

